eration and professional communication. Eating unhealthily may affect reliability (health). B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at weather, excellent computer skills, but sometimes adopts wrong tone, regarded as pretentious, and has weak memory for numbers (attention). B's communication issues may be less severe than A's unfriendly? We need to decide our vote.\n\nWe can argue that A's unfriendly and unhealthy habits raise serious concerns for long-haul flights (crew cooperation, health). B's issues are more manageable. So we might shift recommendation to B.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 2's point and bring our own facts. Provide evidence: A unfriendly, eats unhealthily; B handles stress well, conscientious. Conclude we prefer B.\n\nThus vote Candidate B.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I understand Agent 2's preference for A, but I have concerns about A's unfriendly demeanor and unhealthy eating, which could affect crew cooperation and reliability. In contrast, B is very conscientious, handles stress well, and has good weather assessment, which are crucial. While B has some communication tone issues, they seem less critical than A's interpersonal problems. Therefore I recommend Candidate B.\"\n\nMake sure to reference explicit facts.\n\nNow output."}
